      "writtenOn": "2012-08-19T06:06:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you shouldn\u0027t reset the bedtime each time.  Set the deadline once before starting the loop then just work out how much longer you need to wait from there.\n\nResetting the deadline has problems because timestamps are necessarily imprecise.  Suppose this.wait(duration) always stopped after about 0.9ms.  Then on each iteration, bedtime would be decremented by 0 because a millisecond has not yet elapsed.\n\nThis is unlikely to happen.  Nevertheless, it\u0027s trivial to avoid the problem so we might as well do so.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAIu3///6s\u003d",
